Lab 05: Nested Decision Structures

Aims & Objectives:

Handle multiple conditions using nested decisions.

Simplify complex logic and improve code readability.

Reduce redundancy and create modular programs.

Introduction:
Nested decision structures (if-else, switch-case) allow programs to make hierarchical decisions. Widely used in data processing, games, AI, and business applications.

Key Concepts:

Nested If-Else & Switch-Case

Ternary Operator (condition ? expr1 : expr2)

Operator Precedence

Math Library Functions (<math.h>)

Learning Outcomes:

Implement nested decisions in C.

Write clean, maintainable code.

Apply logical reasoning and math functions effectively.
